        "content": "\n`getArticle`/`getArticleBody` have no tests for the not-found path, and there's no test enforcing that `ARTICLE_BODIES` (in `content/articles/index.ts`) actually has an entry for every slug in `ARTICLES` — currently a silent `?? []` fallback (line 176) would render an empty article body in production if someone adds a new `Article` metadata entry and forgets the body file. Same class of gap for `CATEGORY_GLYPH` vs `CATEGORIES` completeness.\n\n```ts\n// src/lib/articles.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { ARTICLES, ARTICLES_SORTED, CATEGORIES, CATEGORY_GLYPH, getArticle, getArticleBody } from \"./articles\";\n\ndescribe(\"getArticle\", () => {\n  it(\"returns the matching article\", () => {\n    expect(getArticle(\"aifs-india-what-why-trend\")?.category).toBe(\"AIF\");\n  });\n  it(\"returns undefined for an unknown slug\", () => {\n    expect(getArticle(\"does-not-exist\")).toBeUndefined();\n  });\n  it(\"is case-sensitive / does not fuzzy-match\", () => {\n    expect(getArticle(\"AIFS-INDIA-WHAT-WHY-TREND\")).toBeUndefined();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"getArticleBody\", () => {\n  it(\"returns [] instead of throwing for an unknown slug\", () => {\n    expect(getArticleBody(\"nope\")).toEqual([]);\n  });\n  it(\"every ARTICLES entry has a non-empty body — regression guard for the ?? [] fallback\", () => {\n    for (const a of ARTICLES) {\n      expect(getArticleBody(a.slug).length, `missing body for ${a.slug}`).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n    }\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"ARTICLES_SORTED\", () => {\n  it(\"is sorted newest-first by iso date\", () => {\n    const isos = ARTICLES_SORTED.map((a) => a.iso);\n    expect(isos).toEqual([...isos].sort().reverse());\n  });\n  it(\"is a copy, not a mutation of ARTICLES\", () => {\n    expect(ARTICLES_SORTED).not.toBe(ARTICLES);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"CATEGORY_GLYPH\", () => {\n  it(\"has an entry for every non-'All' category\", () => {\n    for (const cat of CATEGORIES.filter((c) => c !== \"All\")) {\n      expect(CATEGORY_GLYPH[cat as keyof typeof CATEGORY_GLYPH]).toBeDefined();\n    }\n  });\n});\n```\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "3. `src/lib/products.tsx` — same shape of gap as articles",
        "content": "\n`getProduct` does an unchecked `slug as ProductSlug` cast (line 522) — behaviorally safe today (unknown key → `undefined`) but untested, and nothing currently proves every `Product.tag` resolves to a real `PRODUCT_GLYPHS` key.\n\n```ts\n// src/lib/products.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { PRODUCTS, getProduct } from \"./products\";\nimport { PRODUCT_GLYPHS } from \"./productGlyphs\";\n\ndescribe(\"getProduct\", () => {\n  it(\"returns the matching product\", () => {\n    expect(getProduct(\"pms\")?.name).toBe(\"Portfolio Management Services\");\n  });\n  it(\"returns undefined for an unknown slug without throwing (unsafe cast at products.tsx:522)\", () => {\n    expect(() => getProduct(\"not-a-real-slug\")).not.toThrow();\n    expect(getProduct(\"not-a-real-slug\")).toBeUndefined();\n  });\n  it(\"returns undefined for empty string\", () => {\n    expect(getProduct(\"\")).toBeUndefined();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"PRODUCTS data integrity\", () => {\n  it(\"every product.tag has a corresponding PRODUCT_GLYPHS entry\", () => {\n    for (const p of PRODUCTS) {\n      expect(PRODUCT_GLYPHS[p.tag], `missing glyph for ${p.tag}`).toBeDefined();\n    }\n  });\n  it(\"slugs are unique\", () => {\n    const slugs = PRODUCTS.map((p) => p.slug);\n    expect(new Set(slugs).size).toBe(slugs.length);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "4. `src/lib/legal.ts` — untested, and a fragile non-null assertion downstream",
        "content": "\n`getLegalDoc` itself is easy to test; the real risk is at the call site: `src/app/privacy-policy/page.tsx:5` does `getLegalDoc(\"privacy-policy\")!` at module scope. If that id is ever mistyped, this throws during the Next.js build for *every* route, not just that page — no test currently catches it.\n\n```ts\n// src/lib/legal.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { LEGAL_DOCS, getLegalDoc } from \"./legal\";\n\ndescribe(\"getLegalDoc\", () => {\n  it(\"resolves each of the four known doc ids\", () => {\n    for (const id of Object.keys(LEGAL_DOCS)) {\n      expect(getLegalDoc(id)).toBeDefined();\n    }\n  });\n  it(\"returns undefined for an unknown id\", () => {\n    expect(getLegalDoc(\"does-not-exist\")).toBeUndefined();\n  });\n  it(\"every doc.path is unique and starts with /\", () => {\n    const paths = Object.values(LEGAL_DOCS).map((d) => d.path);\n    expect(new Set(paths).size).toBe(paths.length);\n    for (const p of paths) expect(p.startsWith(\"/\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "5. `src/app/**/page.tsx` route handlers — integration gap",
        "content": "\nEvery dynamic route (`insights/[slug]`, `products/[slug]`) has three untested behaviors: `generateStaticParams` producing exactly the known slugs, `generateMetadata` returning `{}` for an unknown slug (line 19 in both files), and the page calling `notFound()` for a bad slug. This is exactly the kind of thing that silently regresses when someone renames a slug in `ARTICLES`/`PRODUCTS` but not in a hardcoded link elsewhere.\n\n```tsx\n// src/app/insights/[slug]/page.test.tsx (integration)\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\nimport { generateStaticParams, generateMetadata } from \"./page\";\nimport { ARTICLES } from \"@/lib/articles\";\n\nvi.mock(\"next/navigation\", () => ({ notFound: vi.fn(() => { throw new Error(\"NEXT_NOT_FOUND\"); }) }));\n\ndescribe(\"insights/[slug] route\", () => {\n  it(\"generateStaticParams covers every article slug\", () => {\n    expect(generateStaticParams()).toEqual(ARTICLES.map((a) => ({ slug: a.slug })));\n  });\n  it(\"generateMetadata returns {} for an unknown slug instead of throwing\", async () => {\n    await expect(generateMetadata({ params: Promise.resolve({ slug: \"nope\" }) })).resolves.toEqual({});\n  });\n  it(\"generateMetadata returns title/description for a known slug\", async () => {\n    const meta = await generateMetadata({ params: Promise.resolve({ slug: ARTICLES[0].slug }) });\n    expect(meta.title).toContain(ARTICLES[0].title);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"Page() calls notFound() for an unknown slug — needs a Server Component test harness (RTL doesn't render async RSC directly; consider Playwright hitting a built route)\");\n});\n```\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "6. `buildEnquiry()` in `src/components/pages/ContactPage.tsx` — untested, and not exported",
        "content": "\nLines 34–51: pure logic (trims fields, conditionally appends `product`/`message` lines, joins into a WhatsApp/email body) but it's a module-private function, so it can't be unit-tested in isolation today — that's itself a gap worth fixing (export it, or move it to `src/lib`). Missing edge cases: all-whitespace inputs, missing optional fields, message containing characters that need URL-encoding downstream.\n\n```ts\n// After exporting `buildEnquiry` from ContactPage.tsx:\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { buildEnquiry } from \"./ContactPage\";\n\nfunction fd(entries: Record<string, string>) {\n  const f = new FormData();\n  for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(entries)) f.set(k, v);\n  return f;\n}\n\ndescribe(\"buildEnquiry\", () => {\n  it(\"trims whitespace from all fields\", () => {\n    const { name } = buildEnquiry(fd({ name: \"  Asha  \", email: \"a@b.com\", phone: \"123\" }));\n    expect(name).toBe(\"Asha\");\n  });\n  it(\"omits the product line when product is empty\", () => {\n    const { text } = buildEnquiry(fd({ name: \"A\", email: \"a@b.com\", phone: \"1\", product: \"\" }));\n    expect(text).not.toContain(\"Product of interest:\");\n  });\n  it(\"omits the message line when message is empty\", () => {\n    const { text } = buildEnquiry(fd({ name: \"A\", email: \"a@b.com\", phone: \"1\", message: \"\" }));\n    expect(text).not.toContain(\"Message:\");\n  });\n  it(\"includes product and message when present\", () => {\n    const { text } = buildEnquiry(fd({ name: \"A\", email: \"a@b.com\", phone: \"1\", product: \"PMS\", message: \"Hi\" }));\n    expect(text).toContain(\"Product of interest: PMS\");\n    expect(text).toContain(\"Message: Hi\");\n  });\n  it(\"treats a whitespace-only field as empty (no 'Message: ' line)\", () => {\n    const { text } = buildEnquiry(fd({ name: \"A\", email: \"a@b.com\", phone: \"1\", message: \"   \" }));\n    expect(text).not.toContain(\"Message:\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**Missing error-handling test (real gap, not hypothetical):** `emailInstead` (ContactPage.tsx:91–102) reads `e.currentTarget.closest(\"form\")` and silently `return`s if null, and gates on `form.reportValidity()` — i.e. required fields (`name`, `email`, `phone`) can block the email fallback with no visible feedback beyond native browser validation. No test currently proves that clicking \"Email instead\" with empty required fields does *not* navigate to `mailto:`.\n\n```tsx\n// src/components/pages/ContactPage.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport userEvent from \"@testing-library/user-event\";\nimport ContactPage from \"./ContactPage\";\n\ndescribe(\"ContactPage form\", () => {\n  it(\"does not open mailto: when required fields are empty\", async () => {\n    const user = userEvent.setup();\n    render(<ContactPage />);\n    await user.click(screen.getByText(\"Email instead\"));\n    expect(window.location.href).not.toContain(\"mailto:\");\n  });\n  it(\"submit opens WhatsApp with an encoded message and sets the 'Opening WhatsApp' status text\", async () => {\n    const openSpy = vi.spyOn(window, \"open\").mockImplementation(() => null);\n    const user = userEvent.setup();\n    render(<ContactPage />);\n    await user.type(screen.getByLabelText(/full name/i), \"Test User\");\n    await user.type(screen.getByLabelText(/email address/i), \"t@example.com\");\n    await user.type(screen.getByLabelText(/phone number/i), \"9999999999\");\n    await user.click(screen.getByText(\"Submit via WhatsApp\"));\n    expect(openSpy).toHaveBeenCalledWith(expect.stringContaining(\"wa.me\"), \"_blank\", \"noopener,noreferrer\");\n    expect(await screen.findByText(/Opening WhatsApp/i)).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "7. `RichText.tsx` — render coverage gap",
        "content": "\nPure switch-based renderer over 8 `RichBlock` kinds; no test proves each kind actually renders, and there's a silent-failure risk: the `switch` has no `default` case, so an unrecognized `kind` value (e.g. from a future content type added to `RichBlock` but not handled here) renders nothing with no warning.\n\n```tsx\n// src/components/site/RichText.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport RichText from \"./RichText\";\nimport type { RichBlock } from \"@/lib/content-types\";\n\nconst ALL_KINDS: RichBlock[] = [\n  { kind: \"h2\", text: \"Heading\" },\n  { kind: \"h3\", text: \"Subheading\" },\n  { kind: \"p\", text: \"Paragraph\" },\n  { kind: \"ul\", items: [\"one\", \"two\"] },\n  { kind: \"ol\", items: [\"first\", \"second\"] },\n  { kind: \"quote\", text: \"A quote\" },\n  { kind: \"note\", text: \"A note\" },\n  { kind: \"table\", columns: [\"Col\"], rows: [[\"Cell\"]] },\n];\n\ndescribe(\"RichText\", () => {\n  it.each(ALL_KINDS)(\"renders a $kind block without crashing\", (block) => {\n    expect(() => render(<RichText blocks={[block]} />)).not.toThrow();\n  });\n  it(\"h2 id matches anchorId(text) for in-page TOC links to resolve\", () => {\n    render(<RichText blocks={[{ kind: \"h2\", text: \"What is an AIF?\" }]} />);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"heading\", { level: 2 }).id).toBe(\"what-is-an-aif\");\n  });\n  it(\"renders nothing (not a crash) for an unrecognized block kind — flags the missing default case\", () => {\n    const bogus = { kind: \"bogus\" } as unknown as RichBlock;\n    const { container } = render(<RichText blocks={[bogus]} />);\n    expect(container.textContent).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "8. Stateful client components — no interaction tests",
        "content": "\n- **`InsightsIndex`** (`src/components/pages/InsightsIndex.tsx:70-73`): category filter logic (`active === \"All\" ? ... : filter`) is untested — no test proves clicking a category chip actually narrows the grid, or that switching back to \"All\" restores every article.\n- **`Nav.tsx`**: scroll-state (`scrolled`) toggling at the 48px threshold, and the body-scroll-lock effect (`document.documentElement.style.overflow`) on mobile menu open/close, including the cleanup-on-unmount path — untested.\n- **`Preloader.tsx`**: two divergent code paths (`reduce` vs. animated) both call `onDone()` exactly once via `doneRef` — no test proves `onDone` isn't double-invoked, and no test covers `prefers-reduced-motion` short-circuiting straight to `visible=false`.\n\n```tsx\n// src/components/pages/InsightsIndex.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport userEvent from \"@testing-library/user-event\";\nimport InsightsIndex from \"./InsightsIndex\";\n\ndescribe(\"InsightsIndex category filter\", () => {\n  it(\"shows all articles by default\", () => {\n    render(<InsightsIndex />);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"All\", pressed: true })).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n  it(\"filtering by a category hides non-matching article cards\", async () => {\n    const user = userEvent.setup();\n    render(<InsightsIndex />);\n    await user.click(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"PMS\" }));\n    expect(screen.queryByText(/Why SIF Could Gain/i)).not.toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.getByText(/Portfolio Management Services/i)).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```tsx\n// src/components/Preloader.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport Preloader from \"./Preloader\";\n\ndescribe(\"Preloader\", () => {\n  it(\"calls onDone exactly once, not twice, across the animated path\", async () => {\n    const onDone = vi.fn();\n    render(<Preloader onDone={onDone} />);\n    await vi.waitFor(() => expect(onDone).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1), { timeout: 3000 });\n    await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 500));\n    expect(onDone).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1); // guards doneRef debouncing\n  });\n  it(\"restores documentElement overflow on unmount even if interrupted mid-animation\", () => {\n    const { unmount } = render(<Preloader onDone={() => {}} />);\n    unmount();\n    expect(document.documentElement.style.overflow).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Priority ranking for coverage work",
        "content": "| Priority | Target | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| P0 | Stand up Vitest + RTL | Nothing else can be verified until this exists |\n| P0 | `content-types.ts`, `articles.ts`, `products.tsx`, `legal.ts` | Pure functions, cheap to test, and directly gate what routes render/build |\n| P1 | Route `generateStaticParams`/`generateMetadata`/`notFound()` paths | Regresses silently when slugs drift between data files and links |\n| P1 | `buildEnquiry` + `ContactPage` submit/email flows | Only real \"business logic with error-handling\" in the app; currently unexported and fully untested |\n| P2 | `RichText` render coverage | Cheap, catches the missing-`default`-case silent failure |\n| P2 | `InsightsIndex`, `Nav`, `Preloader` interaction/state tests | Lower risk (cosmetic) but currently the only tested-by-eyeballing behavior in the app |\n\nNo unit-testable \"classes\" exist in this codebase — it's function/component-based throughout, so I scoped this to functions and components accordingly.",
        "level": 3
      }
    ],
    "codeBlocks": [
      {
        "language": "ts",
        "code": "// vitest.config.ts\nimport { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\nimport react from \"@vitejs/plugin-react\";\nimport path from \"path\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [react()],\n  test: { environment: \"jsdom\", globals: true, setupFiles: [\"./vitest.setup.ts\"] },\n  resolve: { alias: { \"@\": path.resolve(__dirname, \"./src\") } },\n});"
      },
      {
        "language": "ts",
        "code": "// src/lib/content-types.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { anchorId, buildToc, readingMinutes, type RichBlock } from \"./content-types\";\n\ndescribe(\"anchorId\", () => {\n  it(\"lowercases and hyphenates\", () => {\n    expect(anchorId(\"What is an AIF?\")).toBe(\"what-is-an-aif\");\n  });\n  it(\"strips punctuation not covered by \\\\w\\\\s-\", () => {\n    expect(anchorId(\"PMS: What & Why\")).toBe(\"pms-what-why\");\n  });\n  it(\"truncates to 60 chars\", () => {\n    const long = \"a\".repeat(100);\n    expect(anchorId(long).length).toBeLessThanOrEqual(60);\n  });\n  it(\"returns empty string for empty input\", () => {\n    expect(anchorId(\"\")).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n  it.todo(\"two headings with identical text produce colliding anchor ids — buildToc should dedupe or the caller should guard against duplicate #hash links\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"buildToc\", () => {\n  it(\"extracts only h2 blocks in order\", () => {\n    const blocks: RichBlock[] = [\n      { kind: \"p\", text: \"intro\" },\n      { kind: \"h2\", text: \"Section One\" },\n      { kind: \"h3\", text: \"sub\" },\n      { kind: \"h2\", text: \"Section Two\" },\n    ];\n    expect(buildToc(blocks)).toEqual([\n      { id: \"section-one\", text: \"Section One\" },\n      { id: \"section-two\", text: \"Section Two\" },\n    ]);\n  });\n  it(\"returns [] when there are no h2 blocks\", () => {\n    expect(buildToc([{ kind: \"p\", text: \"x\" }])).toEqual([]);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"readingMinutes\", () => {\n  it(\"rounds up to a minimum of 1 minute for tiny bodies\", () => {\n    expect(readingMinutes([{ kind: \"p\", text: \"one two three\" }])).toBe(1);\n  });\n  it(\"counts words across p, ul, ol and table blocks\", () => {\n    const blocks: RichBlock[] = [\n      { kind: \"p\", text: \"word \".repeat(100).trim() },\n      { kind: \"ul\", items: [\"a b c\", \"d e f\"] },\n      { kind: \"table\", columns: [\"c1\"], rows: [[\"x y z\"]] },\n    ];\n    expect(readingMinutes(blocks)).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n  });\n  it(\"ignores blocks with no text/items (e.g. quote/note are covered, but a future kind without either would crash)\", () => {\n    // Guards content-types.ts:35-37 which special-cases only \"text\" and \"items\";\n    // a hypothetical new RichBlock variant lacking both silently contributes 0 words.\n    expect(() => readingMinutes([])).not.toThrow();\n  });\n});"
